              "en": "<span style='background:#e0f2fe; color:#0369a1; padding:2px 7px; border-radius:5px; font-weight:800; font-size:12px; margin-right:6px;'>⚡ MEMORIZE</span> <mark style='background:#fef08a; padding:1px 5px; border-radius:3px; font-weight:700;'>The Conceivability Argument (Descartes, Sixth Meditation)</mark>: Premise 1: I can clearly and distinctly conceive of myself as a thinking thing without a physical body. Premise 2: What is clearly conceivable by the intellect is metaphysically possible for God to separate. Conclusion: Mind and body are distinct substances.",
